# u never imports m; the value arrives as a parameter. Chapter 03: "nothing
# has to be imported to read a field — the reader is not a name in your file".
# Gavel 2026-10-12 on #1894: a value carries the arms its type's owner wrote,
# a field of a parameter included, and "a library is checked alone with
# `area x` on a parameter accepted".
#
# Should: print "2..5" on every engine.
# Does: error[name]: no record type has a field `start` (module .../u), on
# check, run and run --interp. Adding `import "../m"` to this file is
# refused as an unused import; reading the fields through a call that names
# m (`h = m/found`) is accepted.
pub fn shown h
  "{h.start}..{h.end}"
